The '''fourth series''' of ''[[The Traitors (British TV series)|The Traitors]]'' was first broadcast on [[BBC One]] on 1 January 2026.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Traitors Series 4 launch date confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/the-traitors-series-4-launch-date-confirmed |website=[[BBC]] |accessdate=12 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=The Traitors season 4: Release date and latest news {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/the-traitors-season-4-release-date/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |accessdate=12 December 2025}}</ref> [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned to present the series, which was accompanied by the spin-off show ''The Traitors: Uncloaked'', presented by [[Ed Gamble]].<ref name="Traitors4">{{cite web |title=The Traitors Series 4 – Everything you need to know |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/articles/2026/the-traitors-series-4 |website=[[BBC]] |accessdate=12 December 2025}}</ref> The series concluded on 23 January 2026 when Rachel Duffy and Stephen Libby won, becoming the first pair of Traitors to win the British version.<ref>{{cite news|last=Youngs|first=Ian|title=The Traitors stars serve up drama in nail-biting final|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c301jg2dlmdo|date=24 January 2026|work=[[BBC News]]|access-date=24 January 2026}}</ref>

==Production==
In August 2024, prior to the beginning of the [[The Traitors (British TV series) series 3|previous series]], it was announced that ''The Traitors'' had been renewed for a fourth series. Applications for the series opened on 22 August 2024, before closing on 28 March 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=How to apply for The Traitors season 4 |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a63391282/the-traitors-season-4/ |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |accessdate=12 December 2025 |date=21 January 2025}}</ref> Filming for the series began in June 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=Your ultimate guide to The Traitors series 4 as start date is announced |url=https://www.hellorayo.co.uk/kiss/entertainment/television/the-traitors-series-4 |website=[[Rayo (streaming)|Rayo]] |accessdate=12 December 2025}}</ref> The first teaser for the fourth series aired at the end of the final of ''[[The Celebrity Traitors]]'', which featured a figure wearing a Traitors' cloak carrying a lantern walking through a forest at night, whilst "[[Heart of Glass (song)|Heart of Glass]]" played in the background.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kanter |first1=Jake |title='The Traitors' Season 4 BBC Premiere Date Revealed |url=https://deadline.com/2025/12/the-traitors-season-4-bbc-premiere-date-1236633012/ |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |accessdate=12 December 2025 |date=2 December 2025}}</ref> The series began on 1 January 2026.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Traitors season four air date confirmed by the BBC |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-traitors-series-four-bbc-b2876524.html |website=[[The Independent]] |accessdate=12 December 2025 |language=en |date=2 December 2025}}</ref>

==Contestants==
The 22 contestants competing in the series were revealed at midnight on 1 January 2026, the day of the show's launch.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Traitors Series 4 Contestants – Meet the players joining Claudia Winkleman in the castle |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/mediapacks/the-traitors-series-4-contestants |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=1 January 2026 |language=en}}</ref> Amongst the contestants were a mother and daughter, Judy and Roxy, and a couple, Ellie and Ross, none of whom revealed their relationships to the other players; Judy and Roxy's connection was revealed to the audience in the first episode, while Ellie and Ross's relationship was revealed to viewers only after Ross's banishment.<ref>{{cite news|last=Sarrubba|first=Stefania|title= Who are Roxy and Judy from The Traitors? Here's what we know about the new parent/child twist|url= https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a69902819/traitors-season-4-roxy-judy/|date=2 January 2026|work=[[Digital Spy]]|access-date=3 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Traitors' Ross gives update on relationship with Ellie after his dramatic exit from the show|first=Sam|last=Warner|work=[[Digital Spy]]|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a69943855/traitors-uk-ross-ellie-now/|date=8 January 2026|access-date=10 January 2026}}</ref> Additionally, Netty and Ross were old acquaintances, who did not know each other would be present and were selected for the series independently; Netty exposed their connection to the other players upon their arrival.<ref>{{cite news|last=Morris|first=Nicky|title=The Traitors stars Netty and Ross's connection explained – despite extensive 'background checks'|url=https://www.hellomagazine.com/film/873198/the-traitors-season-4-netty-ross-connection-explained/|work=[[Hello! (magazine)|Hello! Magazine]]|date=2 January 2026|access-date=2 January 2026}}</ref>

In the first episode, Winkleman revealed that one contestant would be selected as a "Secret Traitor", whose identity would be hidden from both the audience and the regular Traitors. Each night, they would provide the Traitors with a shortlist of Faithful to murder. Contestants were therefore only initially identified as Faithful by appearing on murder shortlists selected by the Secret Traitor, or after being banished. In episode 4, the Secret Traitor was revealed to be Fiona to Traitors Stephen and Rachel after Hugo was banished. Prior to this, the Secret Traitor was visually represented on screen as an unidentified figure dressed in a red cloak.<ref>{{cite web|title=The Traitors Red Cloak Secret Traitor twist explained|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/articles/2026/the-traitors-secret-traitor-red-cloak-explained|date=1 January 2026|website=[[BBC]]|access-date=1 January 2026}}</ref>

